--- A value shows through one display and encodes by one JSON rule, in both
--- modes (docs/bug-classes.md §4). Compiled, a record holding a list, a
--- list of records and a map of them had shown in Rust's debug form, a
--- JSON float as `2.0`, and `str` of a JSON list its JSON text; the
--- interpreter had refused to encode a record, and the compiled program
--- did not build one. An int given a record's float field is a float.
struct P [x, y]
struct L [name, items]
log[L['a', [1, 2]]]
log[[P[1, 2.5], P[3, 4]]]
log[map[a = [P[1, 2]]]]
log[str[L['b', [3]]]]
log['in text: `[P[5, 6]]`']
q = P[1, 2]
log[q.y / 4]
j = json['{"a": [1, 2.0, 2.5, "x"], "n": [1, 2.0], "z": {"k": null}}']
log[j]
log[str[j.a]]
log[keys[j]]
log[has[j, 'z']]
log[encode[j]]
log[encode[P[1, 2.5]]]
log[encode[[L['c', [1.0, 2.0]]]]]
nums = for s in ['1', 'b']
    int[s]
log[encode[nums]]
log[keys[j.n]]
log['not reached']
